WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.580
Hey, this is Presh Talwalkar.

00:00:02.800 --> 00:00:07.919
Consider the points (1, 1) and (2, 2). They can be connected

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:12.050
by the straight line y = x.

00:00:12.920 --> 00:00:18.050
Similarly consider the points (1, 1) and (2, 7).

00:00:18.050 --> 00:00:20.800
They can be connected by the parabola

00:00:20.800 --> 00:00:25.700
y = 2x² - 1. These are

00:00:25.710 --> 00:00:28.380
examples of connecting points with the

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:32.269
polynomial that has integer coefficients.

00:00:32.390 --> 00:00:39.000
Now consider the points (1, 3) and (3, 2).

00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:41.219
Can you connect these points by a polynomial

00:00:41.220 --> 00:00:47.180
that has integer coefficients? That is,

00:00:47.180 --> 00:00:49.530
can you find an equation of the

00:00:49.530 --> 00:00:51.840
following form that passes through the

00:00:51.840 --> 00:00:54.149
two points where all of the coefficients

00:00:54.149 --> 00:00:56.940
are integers meaning they are positive

00:00:56.940 --> 00:01:00.960
or negative whole numbers? If you can,

00:01:00.960 --> 00:01:04.049
find an equation that passes through

00:01:04.049 --> 00:01:07.229
these two points; if you cannot, prove why

00:01:07.229 --> 00:01:11.729
it's impossible to do so. Can you figure

00:01:11.729 --> 00:01:14.790
it out? Give this problem a try, and when

00:01:14.790 --> 00:01:16.530
you're ready, keep watching the video for

00:01:16.530 --> 00:01:19.189
the solution.

00:01:26.340 --> 00:01:29.009
So it would seem you should be able to

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:30.659
find a polynomial that passes through

00:01:30.659 --> 00:01:32.759
these two points because you're not

00:01:32.759 --> 00:01:34.500
restricted to the degree of the

00:01:34.500 --> 00:01:38.369
polynomial. However that turns out to be

00:01:38.369 --> 00:01:41.299
not the case. It is actually impossible

00:01:41.299 --> 00:01:44.219
to find a polynomial with integer

00:01:44.219 --> 00:01:45.899
coefficients that passes through these

00:01:45.899 --> 00:01:49.319
two points. We can, in fact, prove this by

00:01:49.319 --> 00:01:53.819
contradiction. So, let's suppose we have a

00:01:53.819 --> 00:02:00.209
solution. Because this solution passes

00:02:00.209 --> 00:02:02.939
through the point (1, 3), that means

00:02:02.940 --> 00:02:05.440
we can substitute y = 3

00:02:05.440 --> 00:02:09.800
and x = 1. Since 1 raised to any power is

00:02:09.810 --> 00:02:13.530
equal to 1, this simplifies to be 3 is

00:02:13.530 --> 00:02:16.170
equal to the sum of the coefficients and

00:02:16.170 --> 00:02:18.329
we know that each coefficient is an

00:02:18.329 --> 00:02:22.260
integer. So, what we've proven is that the

00:02:22.260 --> 00:02:25.049
sum of these integer coefficients is 3,

00:02:25.049 --> 00:02:31.019
which is an odd number. We also know the

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:32.600
solution would have to pass through the

00:02:32.600 --> 00:02:36.340
point (3, 2), so we can substitute

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:41.220
y = 2 and x = 3. Now we have to

00:02:41.220 --> 00:02:45.389
simplify this a little bit. Consider the

00:02:45.389 --> 00:02:48.900
powers of three. Since three is an odd

00:02:48.900 --> 00:02:51.989
number, and an odd number times an odd

00:02:51.989 --> 00:02:54.870
number is equal to another odd number, we

00:02:54.870 --> 00:02:57.599
can conclude that all powers of three

00:02:57.599 --> 00:03:01.139
are odd numbers so that means three to

00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:05.780
the power of 'k' is always an odd number.

00:03:05.780 --> 00:03:11.489
Furthermore, if the coefficient in a

00:03:11.489 --> 00:03:15.120
particular power is even, then that

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:18.720
coefficient times 3 to the power of k

00:03:18.720 --> 00:03:21.569
will be an even number. This is because

00:03:21.569 --> 00:03:23.790
an even number times any number will be

00:03:23.790 --> 00:03:27.569
an even number. If, on the other hand, the

00:03:27.569 --> 00:03:30.930
coefficient is odd, then the coefficient

00:03:30.930 --> 00:03:33.750
multiplied by 3 to some power will also

00:03:33.750 --> 00:03:35.909
be an odd number, because an odd number

00:03:35.909 --> 00:03:39.100
times another odd number is an odd number.

00:03:40.000 --> 00:03:44.860
So we can conclude that 2 has the same

00:03:44.879 --> 00:03:48.420
evenness or oddness as the sum of the

00:03:48.420 --> 00:03:53.549
coefficients. We can write this in

00:03:53.549 --> 00:03:56.310
another form. We can say that 2 is

00:03:56.310 --> 00:03:59.060
congruent to the sum of the coefficients

00:03:59.060 --> 00:04:04.590
when considering modulo 2. And this

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.919
implies that the sum of the coefficients

00:04:06.920 --> 00:04:11.800
would have to be an even number.

00:04:11.800 --> 00:04:13.880
So on the one hand we have the sum of the

00:04:13.880 --> 00:04:16.080
coefficients being an even number,

00:04:16.080 --> 00:04:17.640
and on the other hand we have the sum of the

00:04:17.640 --> 00:04:21.090
coefficients being an odd number. This is

00:04:21.090 --> 00:04:23.520
impossible; this is a contradiction to

00:04:23.520 --> 00:04:25.440
say that some of the coefficients are

00:04:25.440 --> 00:04:29.360
both even and odd at the same time

00:04:29.360 --> 00:04:31.919
therefore our assumption that we did

00:04:31.919 --> 00:04:34.530
find a solution is not correct, and thus

00:04:34.530 --> 00:04:37.080
there is no such polynomial that can

00:04:37.080 --> 00:04:38.729
pass through these two points with

00:04:38.729 --> 00:04:43.040
integer coefficients. Did you figure it out?

00:04:43.040 --> 00:04:44.610
Thanks for watching this video.

